We have $\mathbf{M} (\mathbf{v} + 3 \mathbf{w}) = \mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} + 3 \mathbf{M} \mathbf{w}.$
Substituting the given values, we have
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{M} (\mathbf{v} + 3 \mathbf{w}) &= \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} + 3 \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -15 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 2-6 \\ 3-15 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix}}.
