If $x=2$ and $y=3$, express the value of the following as a common fraction: $$
\frac
{~\frac{1}{y}~}
{\frac{1}{x}}
$$

solution:
We can simplify the expression by canceling out common terms in the numerator and denominator:
\[\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!} = \frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)(N)(N-1)!} = \frac{1}{N+1}.\]
So the answer is $\boxed{\frac{1}{N+1}}$.The answer is \frac{1}{N+1}

