A function $f$ from the integers to the integers is defined as follows:
\[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n + 3 & \text{if $n$ is odd}, \\
n/2 & \text{if $n$ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Suppose $k$ is odd and $f(f(f(k))) = 27.$  Find $k.$

solution:
We can list out all the possible pairs of numbers: (1,1), (1,2), (1,3), (1,4), (1,5), (2,1), (2,2), (2,3), (2,4), (2,5), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3), (3,4), (3,5), (4,1), (4,2), (4,3), (4,4), (4,5), (5,1), (5,2), (5,3), (5,4), (5,5). Out of these 25 pairs, the pairs that satisfy the condition that the sum of the two numbers is less than their product are (1,1), (1,2), (1,3), (1,4), (1,5), (2,1), (2,2), (2,3), (2,4), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3), (4,1), (4,2), (5,1).
There are 15 pairs that satisfy the condition, so the probability is $\frac{15}{25} = \boxed{\frac{3}{5}}$.
The answer is \frac{3}{5}

