solution:
Let $D$ be the foot of the altitude from $A$ to $\overline{BC}.$  Then $\triangle ABD$ is a 30-60-90 triangle, so $BD = \frac{AB}{2} = 75.$

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

B = (0,0);
A = (3,0);
C = extension(A, A + dir(60), B, B + dir(0));
D = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2;

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D);

label("$A$", A, SE);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, NE);
label("$D$", D, S);
label("$150$", (A + B)/2, S);
label("$50 \sqrt{3}$", (A + C)/2, E);
label("$75$", (B + D)/2, NE);
[/asy]

Then by the Pythagorean Theorem, $BC = \sqrt{150^2 - 75^2} = 75 \sqrt{3}.$

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

B = (0,0);
A = (3,0);
C = extension(A, A + dir(60), B, B + dir(0));
D = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2;

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D);

label("$A$", A, SE);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, NE);
label("$D$", D, S);
label("$150$", (A + B)/2, S);
label("$50 \sqrt{3}$", (A + C)/2, E);
label("$75$", (B + D)/2, NE);
label("$75 \sqrt{3}$", (C + D)/2, NW);
[/asy]

Therefore, the sum of all possible values of $BC$ is $75 \sqrt{3} + 75 \sqrt{3} = \boxed{150 \sqrt{3}}.$The answer is 150\sqrt{3}

