solution:
The cross product of $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} d \\ e \\ f \end{pmatrix}$ is $\begin{pmatrix} bf-ce \\ cd-af \\ ae-bd \end{pmatrix}$.
So the cross product of $\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ is $\begin{pmatrix} (2)(3)-(-6)(1) \\ (-6)(1)-(5)(3) \\ (5)(1)-(2)(1) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ -21 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$.
Therefore, the cross product is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ -21 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}$.The answer is \begin{pmatrix}12\-21\3\end{pmatrix}

