solution:
The equation of the asymptotes is $y = \pm \frac{b}{a} x$.
The slope of the line $y = \frac{b}{a} x$ is $\frac{b}{a}$, so the angle this line makes with the positive $x$-axis is $\arctan \frac{b}{a}$.
Similarly, the angle the line $y = -\frac{b}{a} x$ makes with the positive $x$-axis is $\arctan \frac{b}{a}$ as well.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, P, Q;

A = (-2,0);
B = (2,0);
C = (0,-2);
D = (0,2);
